PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (cols 1-4,6,8-11) converge on A: LP fails both entity routes under NI 45-106. No LP financial statements showing ≥$5M net assets; “all owners are AIs” route blocked because GP (2538901 Ontario Inc.) ownership is unclear after the $6M gift and circular structure among the three individuals. All three LPs individually qualify, but that is insufficient. 

Minority (cols 5,7,12) pick E: argue either net assets fall short after property liabilities or 50/50 ownership by non-AI individuals taints the entity. Counter: GIC $5.5M – $0.3M = $5.2M clearly meets the standalone net-asset test; owner details are irrelevant once the entity test is satisfied.

B meets spousal-income (> $300k combined both years). C meets spousal net-assets (= exactly $5M). D meets entity net-assets ($10M contribution). No unresolved factual gaps on B/C/D. Key open issue: precise scope of “beneficial owners” test for LPs/GPs under 2021 NI 45-106 wording.}

